window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS=(window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Boycott the Owner","paragraphs":["The following morning, Jude woke up in the master stateroom of the ocean liner.","Beyond the window, the Caribbean Sea stretched toward the horizon.","Jude sat up and stretched. During the previous night’s gathering, several models and actresses had approached him, but he had turned them away.","He had little interest in casual distractions when the system interface remained in the corner of his field of view.","The confrontation on the beach had yielded two daily sign-ins alongside a Platinum Reward Box.","\"System,\" Jude said internally. \"Run both sign-ins. Then open the Platinum Reward Box.\"","[Executing Money Sign-Ins...]","[Sign-In 1 Successful! Reward: $45,000,000 USD.]","[Sign-In 2 Successful! Reward: $55,000,000 USD.]","His phone buzzed on the side table as one hundred million dollars routed into his offshore accounts.","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Calculating RNG...]","[Host has acquired three rewards:","[Acquired Skill: Boundless Vitality (Passive).]","[Acquired Asset: $100,000,000 USD Black Card (Restricted: Sapphire Cove Maintenance).]","[Acquired Asset: 100% Exclusive Management Contract (Entity: ’Stellar’).]","Jude paused to review the details.","The passive skill, *Boundless Vitality*, was substantial...","The description indicated that it eliminated the necessity of sleep and cleared mental fatigue.","It removed the ordinary limits of an executive, enabling him to oversee his enterprises without suffering burnout.","The Black Card resolved practical matters.","Managing an island territory and a fleet of vessels required continuous expenditures for upkeep, security, and staff payroll.","The card served as an automated operating fund specifically set aside to cover the running costs of Sapphire Cove.","The third reward caught Jude’s attention...","’Stellar’ was the leading pop group in the domestic market.","The four-member group was an established cultural brand, driving major revenue through tours, merchandise, and commercial endorsements.","Jude opened the contract within his system storage.","Rather than granting a standard share of royalty revenue, it gave him full management control over the group’s professional output and career direction.","Apex Media Group held several corporate subsidiaries, including a music label based in the capital.","Holding direct management authority over the most profitable pop act meant he needed to inspect that branch of the company firsthand.","Spending additional days resting on the coast held little appeal. He preferred active control over passive leisure.","Jude dressed in a charcoal suit and walked out onto the main deck. He found Seraphina Frost holding a drink near the pool.","\"Seraphina,\" Jude said. \"I am returning to the mainland. You are in charge of the event for the rest of the week. Ensure the executives and talent have everything they require.\"","Seraphina set her glass down and stood up. \"You are leaving, Mr. Lawson? The gathering only just began.\"","\"The event is for the staff,\" Jude said. \"I have corporate business to attend to. Tell the crew to prepare the aircraft.\"","Within two hours, Jude was airborne, flying back toward the mainland.","During the flight, he contacted Victoria over a secure channel to ensure the paperwork for the management contract was integrated into Apex Media’s corporate structure.","By afternoon, Jude’s car stopped before the offices of Apex Records... a sixty-story tower of glass situated in the center of the entertainment district.","Rather than notifying the label’s management team to arrange a formal reception, Jude told his driver to remain outside. He chose to enter unannounced to see how the branch operated during ordinary hours, without the staff preparing a display for the owner.","Jude walked through the front doors.","Inside the entrance hall, a wave of noise met him immediately.","The reception floor was crowded. Several hundred young people had gathered across the lobby, blocking the security barriers and the central elevator banks. They carried illuminated signs, light sticks, and promotional boards depicting the four members of *Stellar*.","\"CHLOE! MIA! STELLAR FOREVER!\" a group shouted, holding their signs above the crowd.","Security staff stood near the barriers, trying to keep the crowd back from the inner elevators. Jude observed the room, then moved along the outer perimeter toward the private elevator bank along the far wall.","Before he took five paces, a man in a *Stellar* jacket stepped into his path and shoved him back.","\"Back off, suit,\" the man said. \"No cutting the line. We have been waiting here since four in the morning for the press conference.\"","Jude regained his balance and kept his expression steady. \"I am not here for the press conference. I am heading to the elevators.\"","\"Nobody uses the elevators,\" a woman standing near him said, holding a light stick toward him. \"Not until Apex Records gives us an answer. We are protesting.\"","\"Protesting what?\" Jude asked.","\"You must work for the corporate office,\" the man said. \"Apex Records cannot handle this release. It is a secondary label that has no business managing Stellar’s debut studio album.\"","\"We saw the financial reports,\" another person shouted from the group. \"Apex Media was bought out by an investor who knows nothing about music production. He is going to cut the recording budget and derail the release.\"","Others joined in, taking up the words until a chant echoed through the building.","\"BOYCOTT THE OWNER! SAVE STELLAR!\"","The crowd believed the recent corporate acquisition meant the project would be stripped of capital and creative support...","Jude stood amid the noise, looking at the display screens above the barriers. The monitors showed a countdown timer leading to the scheduled media briefing.","He had arrived to inspect the music division’s operations, only to find the company dealing with a public dispute focused on his purchase of the parent firm.","Jude looked back toward the security gates.","If the public believed Apex Records lacked the capital and scale to manage the production, the upcoming briefing would clarify the matter without ambiguity...","Before Jude could step forward to address the lobby security, a commotion erupted outside the doors of the skyscraper.","A transport SUV with tinted windows had attempted to pull up to the curb.","As the vehicle slowed, an older man in a jacket leaped out from the crowd and threw himself onto the hood of the SUV.","The man screamed, clutching his leg and rolling around as if he had been struck at speed."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: The Ambush","paragraphs":["The vehicle slammed on its brakes. The mob of fans swarmed the SUV, blocking it in.","Jude, with his senses from the Boundless Vitality skill, noticed something wrong.","While the fans were banging on the windows and protesting, four men wearing jackets and surgical masks shoved their way through the crowd.","The four men reached the passenger doors of the SUV. One of them pulled a baton from his jacket, smashing the window.","Another reached inside, grabbing the arm of Lyla, the lead singer of Stellar, attempting to drag her out of the vehicle.","Jude grabbed the nearest man by the collar of his jacket, lifting the thug off his feet, and hurled him backward into a planter. The impact knocked the man out.","The leader of the group, a man wearing mirrored sunglasses, spun around, swinging his baton at Jude’s head.","Jude ducked, the baton whistling inches over his hair.","Jude drove his knee upward into the man’s ribs.","The crack of bone echoed over the screams of the crowd.","As the leader collapsed, Jude planted a shoe onto the side of the man’s head, pinning his skull against the asphalt.","The remaining two thugs froze, looking at Jude standing over their leader. In less than five seconds, a man in a tailored suit had dismantled their ambush.","\"If either of you move a single muscle, I will crush his skull,\" Jude said.","Jude applied a fraction of his weight onto his heel. The man under his shoe let out a shriek as the pressure against his temple became unbearable.","\"Now,\" Jude said, looking down at the leader. \"I am only going to ask this once. Idiots usually don’t get a second chance to answer me. Who is your boss?\"","The man in the sunglasses clawed at the asphalt.","\"Wait! I’ll talk!\" the leader wheezed. \"We’re just contractors! The guy who paid us is Silas Grey!\"","\"Silas Grey,\" Jude repeated, his eyes narrowing. He looked past the shattered window of the SUV, where Lyla was huddled in the backseat. \"Do you know him, Lyla?\"","Lyla shook her head. \"N-no, I’ve never heard of him.\"","\"We don’t know who the ultimate client is!\" the leader groaned, his face grinding against the pavement. \"Silas just gives the orders! But you don’t want to mess with him! He runs the underground fixer network in this city. Let us go, and I’ll tell him you’re off-limits!\"","Jude chuckled. \"You think I’m going to let you go? Get up. You and your men are going to take me directly to Silas Grey.\"","Jude lifted his foot. The leader scrambled backward, gasping for air and clutching his ribs.","He nodded, but a glint flashed behind his mirrored sunglasses.","If this man wanted to walk into Silas Grey’s headquarters, he was signing his own death warrant!","\"Mr. Lawson?\" Lyla’s manager whispered from the driver’s seat, recognizing Jude from the corporate memos. \"Should I call the police?\"","\"Get her inside the building,\" Jude commanded. \"The lobby is secure.\"","Jude turned his attention to the hood of the SUV. The older man who had faked the accident had stopped his groaning. Realizing the kidnapping had failed, the man tried to slide off the hood and disappear into the crowd.","\"Hold it right there,\" Jude said, stepping into his path.","The old man froze, holding up his hands. \"I don’t know them! I was just crossing the street! Your driver hit me!\"","\"My driver was stationary when you threw yourself onto the hood,\" Jude said, pointing to the red recording light of the SUV’s dashcam. \"How much did Silas Grey pay you to orchestrate the blockade?\"","The man’s face went pale. \"N-nothing! I didn’t take any money!\"","Jude held out his hand. \"Give me your identification. Now.\"","The con artist pulled out his wallet and handed over his driver’s license.","Jude pulled out his phone and snapped a photo of the ID card.","\"Your face and your actions are recorded on a dashboard camera,\" Jude said. \"You accepted a bribe to facilitate the kidnapping of a corporate asset. My legal team at Vance & Sterling will ensure you are charged with federal conspiracy. You are looking at a minimum of ten years in a maximum-security prison.\"","The con artist’s knees buckled. He collapsed onto the asphalt, grabbing at Jude’s pant leg. \"Please! I didn’t know they were going to kidnap her! They just told me to stop the car! I beg you, spare me!\"","\"Tell it to the federal judge,\" Jude said, grabbing the man by the collar of his jacket. Jude lifted the man off his feet and threw him onto the sidewalk.","The con artist landed hard, sobbing.","Jude turned to the thugs, who were limping toward an unmarked gray van parked near the curb.","\"Get in,\" Jude ordered, sliding into the back of the van. \"Drive.\"","...","Thirty minutes away, in an abandoned warehouse district on the edge of the city, a man wearing a gold chain sat at a table.","This was Silas Grey...","He was an underground fixer, specializing in corporate sabotage and paparazzi extortion.","He was smoking a Cuban cigar, his phone pressed to his ear.","\"Relax, Pierce,\" Silas said, blowing smoke toward the ceiling. \"I already have a team on the ground outside Apex Records. They are securing the girl as we speak. She won’t be attending any press conferences today.\"","On the other end of the line, Donovan Pierce let out a laugh.","\"Excellent work, Silas,\" Donovan said.","Donovan had been humiliated at the private airport earlier that morning.","He could not attack Jude’s billions directly, but he could sabotage Jude’s newly acquired assets.","\"Once you have her secured, I want you to force her to sign a contract termination. We are going to bleed Apex Media dry.\"","Silas tapped ash onto the floor. \"Forcing an idol to break a contract is tricky, Pierce. I’m going to need double my rate for the legal fallout.\"","Donovan cursed under his breath. Silas was greedy, but Donovan was desperate for revenge.","\"Fine,\" Donovan hissed. \"But if I’m paying double, I want her ruined. Don’t just make her sign the papers. Stage a scandal. Take photos of her in a compromising position.\"","Silas chuckled. \"You’re a sick man, Pierce. But I like your style.\"","\"Stellar’s image is built entirely on their reputation,\" Donovan sneered. \"Lyla is the golden child. If you leak photos of her to the tabloids, her brand dies. Apex Records will lose a hundred-million-dollar IP overnight.\"","\"Consider it done,\" Silas grinned, taking a drag of his cigar. \"My men should be pulling up any minute now.\""]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: True Love","paragraphs":["The doors of the warehouse rolled open The van pulled into the interior and squealed to a halt.","Silas Grey stood up from his table, a grin spreading across his face. He held his phone up to his ear. \"They’re here, Pierce. I’ll call you back when I have the photos.\"","Silas walked over to the back of the van, expecting his men to drag out a pop star.","Instead, the rear doors swung open, and the four thugs tumbled out onto the floor, clutching their ribs.","Silas froze.","Stepping out of the darkness of the van was Jude Lawson.","\"What the hell is this?!\" Silas roared, reaching for the pistol holstered at his hip.","He didn’t even get his hand on the grip. Jude closed the distance with speed.","Jude’s hand shot out, clamping around Silas’s throat, and slammed the fixer backward onto the table.","The phone Silas had been holding clattered onto the surface, the speakerphone still engaged.","\"Silas?\" Donovan Pierce’s voice crackled through the phone speaker. \"What’s going on? Do you have her?\"","Jude kept Silas pinned by the throat with one hand, picking up the phone with the other.","\"Silas is a bit tied up right now, Donovan,\" Jude said.","There was a dead silence on the other end of the line.","\"Lawson?!\" Donovan gasped. \"How... how did you find that number?!\"","\"You really don’t learn, do you?\" Jude chuckled. \"You failed at the private airport, and you failed here. Trying to kidnap my talent is a desperate move.\"","Donovan realized he was caught, but his arrogance refused to let him back down. \"It doesn’t matter, Lawson! Apex Records is absolute garbage! The fans are already boycotting you! Without my studio’s backing, Stellar is going to bleed market value until they jump ship. Your little music division is going to crash and burn!\"","Jude laughed. \"Donovan, I don’t care about market value. If a company burns money, I simply print more. In fact, I am personally injecting two hundred million dollars into Stellar’s contract renewal today. Can your studio match a two-hundred-million-dollar retainer?\"","Donovan’s breath hitched.","\"You’re a maniac!\" Donovan shrieked, his voice cracking before he slammed the phone down, disconnecting the call.","Jude tossed the phone onto the floor, crushing it under his shoe.","He looked down at Silas, who was trembling against the table.","\"The police are about three minutes away,\" Jude said coldly, releasing the fixer’s throat. \"I suggest you have a good lawyer.\"","[Ding!]","[Mission Completed: Crush the Opponent’s Conspiracy.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude ignored the thugs and walked out of the warehouse, hailing a sedan to take him back to the Apex Records skyscraper.","When Jude arrived at the music division’s headquarters, the lobby was secured. The crowd of protesting fans was being held back behind barricades by the police.","Jude bypassed the chaos and entered the secured VIP glass atrium on the ground floor.","Sitting on the sofas was Lyla. Sitting next to her, holding her hand, was Mia. Their manager was pacing in the background.","When Jude walked in, Lyla immediately stood up.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Lyla breathed, tears welling up in her eyes. \"Thank you. If you hadn’t been there...\"","\"It’s handled,\" Jude said, offering a smile. He turned to the manager. \"I assume you have the preliminary contracts for their upcoming renewal cycle?\"","The manager blinked. \"Y-yes, sir. We were preparing a standard two-year extension. Ten million a year for the group.\"","\"Shred it,\" Jude commanded.","The manager froze. \"Sir?\"","\"I want a new contract drafted immediately,\" Jude said, pulling out a pen from his jacket pocket. \"A one-year commitment. And the base salary will be one hundred million dollars for Lyla, and one hundred million dollars for Mia. Furthermore, the contract strictly prohibits any transfer negotiations with Pierce Studios.\"","Lyla and Mia gasped simultaneously. The manager nearly dropped his briefcase...","\"One... one hundred million?\" Mia stammered, her face flushing crimson. \"Each?!\"","\"Mr. Lawson, I feel like that is far too much,\" Lyla protested. \"We are popular, yes, but we aren’t worth a hundred million dollars a year. That kind of budget is unheard of for a single album cycle.\"","Jude looked at the two girls. \"I keep my word. A hundred million is exactly what you are worth to this company. If you think it’s too much, then work hard, get in the studio, and help me earn my investment back.\"","Lyla and Mia looked at each other.","They were used to ruthless corporate executives trying to squeeze every penny out of them. But the billionaire standing in front of them had just risked his life to save them, and was now offering them a financial safety net that would set their families up for generations!","*He must be our biggest fan,* Lyla thought, her cheeks burning hot. *He bought the entire company and fought off thugs just to protect us!*","Lyla and Mia stepped forward.","Before Jude could even register their movement, the two pop stars leaned in from opposite sides and pressed their lips against his cheeks.","\"Thank you, boss,\" Lyla whispered, her voice sweet and genuine. \"We won’t let you down.\"","\"We will work so hard for you,\" Mia added, blushing as she pulled back.","Outside the walls of the VIP atrium, the crowd of protesting fans witnessed the entire exchange.","The fans who had been screaming for Apex Records to burn down suddenly went dead silent.","They stared through the glass, watching their idols kiss the cheeks of the \"evil corporate billionaire.\"","A second later, the crowd lost their minds.","\"NOOO!\" a hardcore fan screamed. \"MY QUEEN! IT CAN’T BE TRUE!\"","\"He bought their love!\" another fan shrieked. \"I’m going to jump off a bridge! This is the worst day of my life!\"","Jude chuckled, reaching up to touch his cheek.","It was obvious the two girls had completely misunderstood his intentions, assuming this was an romantic rescue mission...","Having the loyalty of the nation’s biggest pop stars was exactly what he needed to secure his new music division.","Lyla and Mia stayed close to Jude’s side, whispering excitedly to each other as he led them toward the private executive elevator.","\"I’ve never even seen him in the celebrity magazines,\" Mia whispered, stealing a glance at Jude’s profile. \"How much is he actually worth?\"","\"I read that the true billionaires never appear on the rich lists,\" Lyla whispered back, her eyes shining with admiration. \"He must be one of those hidden titans. We are so lucky.\"","The elevator doors chimed open on the sixtieth floor.","Jude stepped out into the executive suite.","Waiting for him in the central boardroom were the three pillars of Apex Records... Director Vance, Director Chen, and Director Xue.","The executives stood up immediately as Jude entered, their eyes darting between the billionaire and the two idols trailing behind him.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Director Vance said, bowing his head. \"It is an honor. We are at your disposal.\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Celebration","paragraphs":["Jude bypassed the pleasantries, walking straight to the head of the boardroom table.","He took a seat in the executive chair, gesturing for the three directors to sit.","Lyla and Mia quietly took seats near the corner, trying to make themselves as small as possible in the presence of the label’s highest authorities.","\"Let’s cut right to the operational metrics,\" Jude said. \"I want a blunt assessment of the music division’s current talent roster and its operating capital.\"","Director Vance adjusted his tie. \"Of course, Mr. Lawson. I won’t sugarcoat it. Currently, Apex Records is running a very lean roster. We have two solid B-list solo artists who generate consistent streaming revenue. Beyond them, we have about forty indie and tertiary acts on short-term developmental contracts.\"","\"And the financials?\" Jude asked.","\"We have several stadium tours in production,\" Director Xue chimed in, opening a ledger. \"The upfront investment for staging, marketing, and logistics is draining our reserves. Last fiscal year, despite grossing a respectable amount, the division’s actual net profit was a meager forty million dollars.\"","For a localized studio, it would be a success. But for the music division of a multi-billion-dollar media conglomerate, it was essentially pocket change...","Director Chen, the oldest of the three executives, let out a sigh and looked toward Lyla and Mia.","\"Mr. Lawson, forgive me for speaking out of turn,\" Director Chen began carefully. \"But your assistant informed us downstairs that you authorized a two-hundred-million-dollar contract renewal for Stellar. Given our forty-million-dollar net profit... that contract is financially ruinous. We simply do not have the operating capital to absorb a two-hundred-million-dollar salary payout without bankrupting the entire division’s ledger.\"","Lyla and Mia visibly flinched.","Facing the judgment of the veteran directors, the two pop stars lowered their heads, feeling out of place.","They were artists, not corporate strategists...","In the eyes of the board, they were suddenly a massive financial liability.","Mia chewed her bottom lip nervously, looking over at Jude with a pleading expression.","Jude looked at Director Chen. \"If the current operating capital is insufficient to support my artists, Director Chen, then the solution is simple,\" Jude stated smoothly. \"I will rewrite the ledger.\"","The three directors stared at him.","\"I am officially authorizing a personal capital injection into Apex Records,\" Jude announced, leaning back in his chair. \"I will provide an additional one billion dollars annually, entirely dedicated to roster development and studio expansion. Do you possess the administrative capability to manage a billion-dollar development fund, or do I need to find a new board of directors?\"","The boardroom fell into silence.","Director Vance stared at Jude as if the young man had just offered to personally fund a space program.","\"One... one billion dollars?\" Director Xue stammered. \"Annually?!\"","\"Your base corporate valuation was just over two billion when I bought the conglomerate,\" Jude said, pulling out his smartphone. \"Adding a billion in liquid capital gives you the leverage to dominate the industry.\"","Jude accessed his offshore accounts through his encrypted interface. With a few taps on the screen, he routed five hundred million dollars straight into Apex Records’ corporate account as a six-month down payment.","Ten seconds later, the tablet sitting in front of Director Chen chimed.","The director looked down at the banking notification. His face went pale. The influx of capital had already cleared.","\"It’s... it’s here,\" Director Chen whispered in awe.","Director Vance let out a booming laugh, his demeanor shifting from cautious to sycophantic.","\"Mr. Lawson, your liquidity is terrifying!\" Director Vance praised. \"With a billion-dollar war chest, all of our logistical bottlenecks vanish overnight! We can outbid every major label on the continent!\"","Director Chen immediately turned toward Lyla and Mia, offering them an apologetic smile.","\"I completely retract my previous statement,\" Director Chen said. \"Lyla, Mia, you two are generational talents. You are the core of this label’s future. With Mr. Lawson’s funding, we will launch a global marketing campaign that will make your previous tours look like local theater.\"","Lyla and Mia let out a sigh of relief. They looked at Jude with profound loyalty.","He hadn’t just protected their contract; he had bent the board of directors to his will just to secure their future!","Jude slipped his phone back into his pocket.","\"Since the financial restructuring is settled,\" Director Vance said, standing up. \"I believe it is imperative that we formally introduce you to the rest of the roster, Mr. Lawson. The artists need to see the man who is about to revolutionize their careers.\"","Ten minutes later, Director Vance had called an assembly in the label’s acoustic training hall.","Over fifty signed artists, ranging from indie producers to established pop vocalists, had been pulled from their recording booths and dance rehearsals.","Standing near the front row of the assembly were the label’s two most prominent mid-tier artists...","A platinum-selling R&B vocalist named Orion, and a popular electro-pop singer named Elena.","\"If the rumors are true, this is the best thing that could have happened to us,\" Orion said confidently, adjusting his jacket. \"Apex Records was bleeding cash on those stadium tours. We needed a billionaire to step in.\"","\"Quiet,\" Elena hissed, nodding toward the doors at the back of the hall. \"They’re coming.\"","The doors swung open.","Jude walked into the acoustic training hall, flanked by the three senior directors and the two idols of Stellar.","Every artist in the hall stared at Jude in shock. They had expected a gray-haired, Wall Street tycoon in a stuffy suit. Instead, they were looking at a handsome young man.","\"My god, he’s so young,\" Elena whispered, her eyes wide.","Director Vance stepped up to the microphone stand at the center of the room.","\"Ladies and gentlemen, it is my honor to introduce you to the sole owner of Apex Records, Mr. Jude Lawson,\"","\"And I am thrilled to announce that Mr. Lawson has just authorized an annual, one-billion-dollar capital injection into this label’s development fund!\"","The training hall exploded.","It was a tidal wave of pure cheering...","Dancers, singers, and producers screamed in excitement.","A billion dollars meant endless recording budgets, massive promotional tours, and top-tier production equipment...","The new boss hadn’t come to slash their contracts; he had come to elevate them all to superstardom!","Orion and Elena stepped forward from the front row.","\"Mr. Lawson, it is an honor,\" Orion said smoothly, offering a bow. \"Your vision for this label is incredible. We are at your service.\"","\"We would love to properly celebrate your arrival, Mr. Lawson,\" Elena added, flashing a smile as she stepped closer. \"Orion and I would be honored to host a welcome banquet for you tonight at the Obsidian Grand. The entire senior roster will be there to celebrate the new era of Apex Records.\"","The surrounding artists cheered their agreement, desperate for a chance to network with the billionaire.","Jude looked at the eager, expectant faces of his newly acquired talent.","He had spent the morning dismantling a kidnapping and restructuring a corporation...","A celebration at the city’s most exclusive hotel sounded like the perfect way to conclude the day.","\"I accept,\" Jude said. \"Set it up.\""]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: The Chairman","paragraphs":["The Diamond Ballroom at the Obsidian Grand Hotel was reserved for Apex Records.","By nine o’clock that evening, the hall was filled with the label’s top artists, producers, and executives.","Jude sat at the center of the VIP table, nursing a glass of bourbon.","\"Mr. Lawson, to celebrate your arrival, we thought we should demonstrate exactly what kind of talent you’ve invested in,\" Elena announced, stepping into the open space in front of the VIP table.","Elena was wearing a backless crimson dress. As the ballroom’s acoustic band began to play a slow bassline, Elena launched into a choreographed dance routine.","She was a professional through and through, but it was obvious to everyone in the room that this was a targeted performance...","Every single time Elena twirled or struck a pose, her eyes locked onto Jude, flashing him lingering looks.","It was a blatant attempt to seduce the new billionaire owner.","Sitting on the sofa behind Jude, Lyla and Mia watched the performance with narrowing eyes.","\"She is shameless,\" Mia whispered to Lyla, her jaw clenching. \"She’s practically throwing herself at him.\"","Lyla nodded, feeling a spike of jealousy.","Jude had risked his life to save them from thugs earlier that day. He had given them a hundred million dollars each.","In Lyla’s mind, Jude was *their* savior, and she wasn’t about to let an opportunistic pop star steal his attention.","\"We are not letting her outshine us,\" Lyla whispered.","As soon as Elena finished her routine to a round of polite applause, Lyla and Mia immediately stood up, smoothing out their designer dresses.","\"That was beautiful, Elena,\" Lyla said, stepping past the other singer to take the floor. \"But we would also like to offer Mr. Lawson a proper welcome.\"","The ballroom grew quiet as the two most famous idols in the country took their positions.","Lyla and Mia didn’t need a heavy bassline or a sultry dance routine. They signaled the acoustic guitarist, and as a melodic chord filled the room, the two girls began to sing.","Their voices harmonized with perfection. It was an acoustic rendition of their biggest chart-topping hit, but stripped of the studio production, the power of their vocals was undeniable.","Throughout the song, Lyla and Mia kept their gaze locked on Jude, singing the lyrics directly to him.","Jude swirled his bourbon, an amused smile touching his lips.","He could clearly see the competitive tension between the female artists, but watching the nation’s top talent battle for his favor was an entertaining way to spend the evening...","Just as Lyla hit the final high note of the chorus, a crash echoed through the room.","The doors of the Diamond Ballroom were shoved open, slamming against the walls.","The music ground to a halt. The Apex Records artists turned in shock as a tall man in a silver suit marched into the ballroom, flanked by bodyguards and rival executives.","\"Well, isn’t this adorable?\" the man sneered. \"The Wall Street billionaire buys a new toy and immediately sets up a private harem for himself.\"","Director Vance, who was sitting next to Jude, went pale. He leaned in, his voice trembling.","\"Mr. Lawson, that is Derrick Vanguard,\" Director Vance whispered. \"He is the Chairman and majority shareholder of Vanguard Records. They are our fiercest corporate rivals in the city.\"","Derrick Vanguard strutted toward the center of the room, his eyes scanning the crowd with disdain.","When his gaze landed on Elena, a smile spread across his face.","\"Elena, darling,\" Derrick said, extending a hand toward her. \"I told you last month that you belong at a real label. Pack up your things. Vanguard Records is formally offering to buy out your contract right now.\"","Elena frowned, crossing her arms.","\"What kind of future do you think you have here?\" Derrick laughed, gesturing toward Jude. \"Your new boss is an absolute layman. He’s a clueless finance suit who doesn’t know the first thing about the music industry. I heard the rumors, Lawson! You authorized two hundred million dollars for Stellar?!\"","Derrick pointed at Lyla and Mia, scoffing loudly. \"Two hundred million for two girls whose brand is already stalling! It’s the most amateur business decision I’ve ever seen!\"","Lyla flinched, her hands balling into fists.","Elena didn’t hesitate. She glared at Derrick and took three steps backward, intentionally placing herself behind Jude’s chair.","\"I respectfully decline your offer, Mr. Vanguard,\" Elena said. \"I am happy with Apex Records.\"","Derrick’s smug smile faltered, his eyes flashing with irritation at the public rejection. But he quickly recovered, letting out a sigh.","\"Suit yourselves,\" Derrick boasted, turning to address the entire ballroom of Apex artists. \"I was trying to throw you a lifeline before your company sinks. Because as of an hour ago, Vanguard Records has officially acquired exclusive, lifetime management rights to *The Velvet 32*.\"","A collective gasp echoed through the Diamond Ballroom.","Even Director Vance let out a choked breath, his hands shaking as he gripped the edge of the VIP table.","\"The Velvet 32?\" Orion whispered, staring at Derrick in disbelief. \"That’s impossible. They are an independent supergroup!\"","Derrick fed off the shock in the room. \"Not anymore! We bought them out completely!\"","The Velvet 32 was an absolute juggernaut in the entertainment industry...","They were a massive supergroup consisting of thirty-two multi-talented performers.","They dominated television ratings, social media metrics, and streaming charts. Their global fanbase was estimated at over forty million people!","\"Do you understand what this means, Lawson?\" Derrick sneered, looking down at Jude. \"With the Velvet 32 under my control, Vanguard Records holds a monopoly over the pop market. The volume of their fanbase allows me to dictate industry trends. I can make anyone a star, and I can crush anyone who stands in my way!\"","Several of the indie artists and backup dancers in the back of the room exchanged nervous glances.","The power to leverage a forty-million-person fanbase was unprecedented...","Being signed to Vanguard Records suddenly looked like a guaranteed ticket to international fame.","Derrick Vanguard had crashed the party for one specific reason: to break the Apex Records roster and assert his dominance over the new billionaire.","Jude remained seated. He took a sip of his bourbon.","Before Jude could respond to the Chairman, a familiar chime rang clearly in his mind.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Unrivaled Stardom.]","[Objective: A rival label is attempting to leverage a forty-million-fan supergroup to undermine your corporate authority and poach your talent. Show them that their supergroup is nothing but a localized fad. Prove the absolute dominance of your own assets.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude lowered his glass. A smile slowly crept across his face.","The system wanted him to crush Derrick Vanguard’s newly acquired pride and joy. And Jude knew exactly how to do it."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Supergroup","paragraphs":["\"A massive supergroup, Derrick?\" Jude said. \"What an interesting coincidence. I also happened to acquire a collective recently.\"","Derrick blinked, then threw his head back and let out a laugh.","\"You?\" Derrick mocked, looking around at his executives, who joined in the laughter. \"What did you buy, Lawson? A struggling indie choir from a community college? A washed-up boy band from the nineties?\"","Derrick stepped closer to the VIP table, leaning on the back of an empty chair. \"You clearly don’t understand the capital required to play at this level. I spent two billion dollars to acquire the exclusive management rights to the Velvet 32! It is an asset class that Wall Street suits can’t even comprehend. An entertainment collective of that magnitude is a billion-dollar star-making engine!\"","To him, the Velvet 32 was an unstoppable juggernaut that placed Vanguard Records at the pinnacle of the industry.","Director Vance leaned closer to Jude.","\"Mr. Lawson, you didn’t mention another acquisition during the board meeting,\" Director Vance whispered. \"What team did you buy? A forty-million-fan collective is incredibly difficult to combat in the current media cycle.\"","Orion stepped closer to the table.","\"There’s only one group in the world that can completely eclipse the Velvet 32,\" Orion muttered. \"The Sirens. They are an eighty-eight-member global collective. They have three A-list megastars anchoring the team, and their combined fanbase is pushing eighty million across all platforms.\"","Elena gasped. \"Eighty million? That’s double the Velvet 32. But they are untouchable.\"","Derrick Vanguard’s ears caught Orion’s conversation. He barked out another cruel laugh.","\"The Sirens?\" Derrick scoffed, shaking his head. \"Don’t even dream about it! Vanguard Records offered their parent company three billion dollars last quarter for a fifty-percent stake. You know what they did? They laughed and hung up on me! Nobody in this industry has the capital to acquire The Sirens. They are a sovereign entity in the music world!\"","The Apex Records artists sighed.","If a titan like Derrick Vanguard couldn’t buy his way into The Sirens with three billion dollars, it was an impossible dream...","The Velvet 32 would remain the undisputed kings of the industry.","Jude swirled the amber liquid in his glass, amused by Derrick’s grandstanding.","\"They hung up on you, Derrick?\" Jude asked, a smirk playing on his lips. \"That doesn’t surprise me.\"","\"And why is that, Lawson?\" Derrick challenged, crossing his arms.","\"Because they were waiting for a real offer,\" Jude stated. \"When I dropped a billion dollars into my development fund this afternoon, I also had my acquisitions team execute a hostile buyout of their parent company. I didn’t offer for a fifty-percent stake. I bought them outright.\"","The Diamond Ballroom fell into silence.","The clinking of champagne glasses ceased. The acoustic guitarist in the corner dropped his pick onto the floor, the tiny *click* sounding like a gunshot in the room.","Derrick Vanguard’s smug expression shattered.","The blood drained from his face as his brain tried to process Jude’s claim.","\"You... you bought The Sirens?\" Director Vance choked out.","\"You’re lying!\" Derrick screamed, his voice cracking. \"That is a lie! You did not buy The Sirens! You’re just trying to save face in front of your artists because I humiliated you!\"","Derrick pointed a shaking finger at Jude’s chest. \"I see through you, Lawson! You think you can just drop a name and everyone will bow down to you? If you actually own The Sirens, prove it!\"","\"I don’t need to prove anything to you, Derrick,\" Jude replied.","\"Call them!\" Derrick challenged, his face turning red. \"If you are the sole owner of the eighty-eight-member supergroup, then you have their management on speed dial! Call them right now! Have them walk into this hotel!\"","Derrick was breathing heavily. \"If you can summon The Sirens to this ballroom tonight, I will drop to my knees in front of your entire roster and beg for your forgiveness! But when they don’t show up, I am going to expose you as the fraud you are!\"","Jude raised an eyebrow. \"You want to drop to your knees? By all means, Derrick. Let me facilitate that for you.\"","Without breaking eye contact with the furious CEO, Jude reached into the inner pocket of his jacket and pulled out his smartphone. He scrolled to an encrypted contact list.","He tapped the screen, placing the call on speakerphone and setting the device down on the polished mahogany table.","The phone rang twice before it was picked up.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" a crisp female voice answered. \"This is the Executive Director for The Sirens. It is an honor to speak with you. We received the finalized buyout paperwork this afternoon. The entire collective is at your disposal.\"","The Apex Records artists gasped. Derrick Vanguard’s eyes went wide.","\"Director,\" Jude said calmly. \"I am currently hosting a welcome banquet at the Diamond Ballroom in the Obsidian Grand Hotel. Gather the entire eighty-eight-member team. I want them here immediately.\"","\"Right away, Mr. Lawson!\" the Director replied without hesitation. \"The team is currently at their downtown recording compound. We will load the transport fleet and be at the Obsidian Grand in twenty minutes.\"","Jude tapped the screen, ending the call. He looked up at Derrick, whose face was a mask of horror.","\"Twenty minutes,\" Jude said, taking a sip of his bourbon. \"I suggest you stretch your knees, Derrick. The floor looks quite hard.\"","Derrick stumbled backward. He looked at his rival executives, who were paralyzed with fear.","If Jude Lawson truly owned The Sirens, Vanguard Records was obsolete...","The Velvet 32 was a massive asset, but compared to the global juggernaut of The Sirens, they were practically a garage band.","Derrick turned toward Elena.","\"Elena, listen to me,\" Derrick pleaded, his voice stripped of arrogance. \"This guy is a maniac! He’s going to bankrupt this entire conglomerate! My offer still stands. Walk out of this hotel with me, and I will double your base salary at Vanguard!\"","Elena didn’t look at him. She crossed her arms, her eyes locked on Jude with admiration.","\"I already told you, Mr. Vanguard,\" Elena said. \"I am perfectly happy with my boss.\"","The rest of the Apex Records roster remained silent, watching Derrick panic.","In twenty minutes, the biggest supergroup on the planet was going to walk through the doors..."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Backfire","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, earlier that afternoon across town, inside the executive boardroom of Pierce Studios...","Donovan Pierce was nursing a glass of scotch, a smirk resting on his face. Surrounding him were the studio’s top shareholders and vice presidents.","\"Gentlemen, you can put your concerns regarding Apex Records to rest,\" Donovan announced, raising his glass. \"I have it on good authority that their music division is about to suffer a catastrophic PR disaster. Their lead asset is compromised.\"","\"Are you certain, Donovan?\" a vice president asked cautiously. \"Lawson just injected capital into the conglomerate. If Stellar renews their contracts, Apex will dominate the Q3 charts.\"","\"They aren’t renewing anything,\" Donovan laughed, taking a sip of his scotch. \"Trust me, the girl’s brand is about to be ruined.\"","Donovan felt a rush of satisfaction. Silas Grey was a professional.","By now, the photos were probably being shopped around to the tabloids...","Apex Records was going to burn, and Jude Lawson’s billion-dollar investment would go up in smoke.","\"Prepare a press release,\" Donovan commanded, waving his hand. \"When the scandal breaks, I want Pierce Studios positioned to absorb their sponsorships. It’s a two-birds-one-stone strategy.\"","\"Sir?\"","One of the executives at the end of the table spoke up, his voice trembling.","He was staring at the television mounted on the boardroom wall, which was tuned to a news network.","\"What is it?\" Donovan snapped.","\"I... I don’t think she’s resigning, sir,\" the executive stammered, pointing a finger at the screen.","Donovan frowned and turned his head.","The television screen was broadcasting a live feed from the VIP atrium of Apex Records.","Standing in the center of the room, looking radiant and unharmed, were Lyla and Mia.","The headline banner scrolling across the bottom of the screen read:","BREAKING: APEX RECORDS SECURES STELLAR WITH UNPRECEDENTED $200 MILLION RENEWAL CONTRACT.","On the screen, Lyla was smiling for the cameras, holding up a signed corporate binder.","Donovan Pierce’s eyes bulged out of his head. He spit out a mouthful of scotch, the liquid spraying across the table.","\"What?!\" Donovan shrieked, his voice cracking.","He stared at the screen, his brain short-circuiting.","*How is she standing in that lobby?!* Donovan’s mind screamed. *Wasn’t she supposed to be locked inside Silas Grey’s warehouse?!*","***","Later that night, high above the city in the penthouse suite of the Obsidian Grand...","\"You are actually terrifying when you want to be, Jude,\" Maya’s voice crackled through the phone line. \"I just saw the financial blogs. Derrick Vanguard’s stock is already tanking in aftermarket trading.\"","Jude stood by the windows of his penthouse suite at the top of the Obsidian Grand, looking out over the glittering city skyline.","The banquet had been a legendary success...","When The Sirens had arrived, Derrick Vanguard had fled the hotel.","Jude sighed. \"Tomorrow morning, when I officially sign the integration contracts, Apex Media and Zenith Motors will be unstoppable. Every piece of the board is moving exactly as calculated.\"","Maya laughed, her voice filled with admiration. \"I never doubted you for a second. The way you restructure these massive conglomerates is on another level.\"","\"I appreciate that,\" Jude said, feeling a wave of warmth. \"Speaking of tomorrow, are you still planning to review the new Zenith expansion ledgers in person?\"","\"Absolutely,\" Maya said, her excitement palpable. \"I’ll be at the penthouse first thing in the morning. I need to see exactly how you plan to merge our logistics with Apex’s new talent contracts.\"","\"Perfect,\" Jude smiled. \"I’ll have the blueprints ready. Have a good night, Maya.\"","\"You too, boss,\" she replied, ending the call.","Jude slipped his phone into his pocket.","He had conquered the domestic entertainment market in a single afternoon, and tomorrow would solidify his empire... But for now, he needed to decompress.","He walked over to the digital intercom mounted on the wall and pressed the direct line to the hotel’s head concierge.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" the concierge answered instantly. \"How may we serve you tonight?\"","\"I’ve had a long day,\" Jude said. \"Have the head chef prepare a Wagyu ribeye, seared rare, along with a bone broth. I want it sent up to the penthouse in one hour.\"","\"Consider it done, sir. We will begin preparation immediately.\"","Jude severed the connection and headed toward the master bathroom. He stripped off his suit and stepped into the shower, cranking the temperature dial all the way to cold.","After ten minutes of silence under the freezing spray, Jude stepped out, drying off with a towel.","He bypassed his collection of bespoke suits, opting instead for a pair of dark tactical cargo pants and a fitted black shirt.","Feeling refreshed, Jude made his way down the floating glass staircase to the penthouse’s private screening room.","The theater was a masterpiece of modern design...","Jude sank into the center recliner, picking up the remote. He bypassed the financial news networks and flipped the channel to a live broadcast of an underground mixed martial arts championship.","The arena lights were bright on the screen. The two fighters stepping into the hexagonal cage were a study in contrast.","One was a hulking brawler. The other was a lean striker, built for speed.","\"Ladies and gentlemen!\"","\"Tonight, we witness the ultimate clash of styles for the undisputed title!\"","Jude leaned back, watching intently.","The massive brawler charged forward with brute strength, throwing looping hooks.","But the leaner fighter used his agility to slip under the onslaught, delivering a kick to the back of the giant’s knee.","The crowd on the screen roared as the big man staggered, but he recovered instantly, grabbing the smaller fighter by the waist and slamming him into the canvas with a crash.","Jude winced slightly.","The brawler fought exactly like Donovan Pierce and Derrick Vanguard...","As the match dragged into the later rounds, the lean fighter weathered the storm.","He absorbed the punishment, waited for the giant to overextend, and then struck with surgical precision.","In a stunning reversal, the tactical fighter slipped his hips, wrapped his legs around the giant’s neck, and locked in a triangle choke.","The giant thrashed, using all his remaining strength to break the hold.","A few seconds later, the brawler tapped the mat in defeat.","Jude slowly clapped his hands in the theater, appreciating the victory.","Seeking a change of pace, Jude flipped the channel to a horror film.","The movie opened with a chilling orchestral score. The setting was a Victorian mansion, isolated in a rainstorm. A group of college students arrived at the estate.","Jude watched as the characters began making every illogical decision imaginable.","They willfully ignored the warning signs on the gates. They split up to explore the unlit basement.","When the power was cut, rather than grouping together to secure a perimeter, they wandered into the shadows.","The cinematic tension was supposed to be terrifying. Supernatural entities began picking the students off one by one. But Jude was profoundly annoyed.","After twenty minutes of watching a teenager slowly back into a dark closet while a monster was standing right behind her, Jude couldn’t take it anymore...","He hit the power button, plunging the theater into darkness.","Jude sighed, shaking his head. \"I’ll stick to the financial markets.\"","Sitting in the quiet darkness of the theater, Jude’s mind pivoted away from the screen and back to the true layout of his growing empire.","He closed his eyes, visualizing the blueprints for the new Zenith Motors headquarters he planned to build in the city’s commercial district.","He pictured a towering, sleek monolith of black glass and steel that would overshadow the surrounding corporate skyline.","Jude wouldn’t rely on standard corporate guards. He would contract elite private military firms to secure the perimeter.","He saw himself expanding beyond the domestic borders. With The Sirens under his control, he had a direct pipeline into the global entertainment market.","A sharp knock echoed through the penthouse.","Jude’s eyes snapped open. The food wasn’t due for another thirty minutes, and the concierge always called before sending staff up to the private floor.","\"Who is it?\" Jude called out."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Entertainment Industry","paragraphs":["\"It’s Maya, Jude,\" a voice called through the door. \"And I have Director Vance from Apex Records with me. I apologize for the late intrusion, but we have a time-sensitive emergency.\"","Jude crossed the room and unlocked the door. Maya was standing in the hallway holding a tablet. Beside her, Director Vance looked on the verge of a panic attack.","\"Come in,\" Jude said, gesturing toward the living area of the penthouse. \"What is the emergency?\"","\"It’s the Global Soundwave Network, Mr. Lawson,\" Director Vance explained, following Jude into the room. \"They are the largest international streaming conglomerate in the world. Once a year, they hold a blind digital auction for ten headliner spots across their entire global platform. Winning those spots guarantees international superstardom.\"","Maya set the tablet down on the coffee table. The screen displayed a digital bidding lobby.","\"Derrick Vanguard lodged a bid of two hundred million dollars for the ten spots,\" Maya said. \"The auction closes in three minutes. He’s buying them to lock Apex Records out of the global market. If we lose this auction, our artists won’t get premium placement on any international streaming playlist for a year.\"","Jude looked at the tablet. He could see rival entertainment tycoons creeping the price up.","\"Two hundred million?\" Jude mused. He sat down on the leather sofa. \"Derrick plays far too small.\"","Jude reached out, pulled the tablet toward him, and tapped the digital entry pad.","He didn’t bother calculating a competitive counter-offer. He authorized a bid from his offshore accounts.","He typed in a flat $1,000,000,000.","He hit submit.","The digital auction lobby on the screen instantly froze. The scrolling feed of corporate bids stopped dead.","Director Vance stared at the tablet, his eyes bulging. \"One... one billion dollars?! Even if the ten spots guarantee international fame, the return on investment from streaming revenue won’t even cover thirty percent of that bid! It’s a massive loss!\"","Jude leaned back, unconcerned. \"Director Vance, do I look like a man who cares about a seventy percent deficit on a marketing expense? I don’t care about the return on investment.\"","On the screen, the other representatives were dumbfounded. No one dared to lodge a counter-bid against a billion dollars.","Ten seconds later, the tablet chimed. The network executives at Global Soundwave accepted the bid and locked the auction.","\"They accepted,\" Maya whispered in awe.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Completed: Unrivaled Stardom.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude smiled faintly.","He had an omnipotent financial system backing him...","Spending a billion dollars to crush Derrick Vanguard was worth it.","\"Director Vance,\" Jude said, standing up. \"The spots are secured. I will see you at the studio tomorrow morning to finalize the talent allocations.\"","\"Y-yes, Mr. Lawson. Thank you!\" Director Vance bowed and hurried out of the penthouse.","Jude mentally accessed his system interface.","\"System, execute the money sign-in,\" Jude commanded.","[Sign-In Successful! Reward: $60,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In Successful! Reward: $50,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In Successful! Reward: $150,000,000 USD.]","Jude felt his phone buzz.","Nearly three hundred million dollars had just been deposited into his accounts. He had just spent a billion, and the system had instantly refunded a third of it.","\"Now,\" Jude thought. \"Open the Platinum Reward Box.\"","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Congratulations, Host! You have acquired three premium rewards!]","[Acquired Skill: Absolute Discernment (Passive).]","[Acquired Skill: Flawless Oration (Passive).]","[Acquired Assets: Three $100,000,000 USD Corporate Slush Funds (Categories: Digital Media, Luxury Real Estate, Bespoke Assets).]","The *Absolute Discernment* skill was fascinating...","The system detailed that he would now be able to instantly recognize the difference between natural authenticity and artificial enhancement... whether it was a person’s appearance, the structural integrity of a building, or the hidden clauses in a corporate contract. Nothing could be hidden from his gaze!","The *Flawless Oration* skill upgraded his vocal resonance and public speaking abilities.","His words would now naturally command the attention of any audience.","Possessing the ability to dominate a crowded press conference or a hostile shareholder meeting was a powerful weapon...","The three slush funds were the cherry on top. He now had three hundred million dollars earmarked for expansion.","...","The following morning, Jude arrived at the Apex Records skyscraper to allocate the ten global streaming spots.","The moment he stepped into the ground-floor lobby, he realized Director Vance had leaked the news of the auction to the entire talent roster.","The lobby was packed with every artist signed to the Apex conglomerate.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" an actress pleaded, pushing her way to the front of the mob. \"My international demographics perfectly align with the Global Soundwave network! Please, I just need one spot!\"","\"Boss, I will do anything for a placement!\" a pop star yelled, throwing herself at Jude’s chest.","With his newly acquired skills active, Jude scanned the crowd.","He could instantly see the artificiality in their desperate smiles, the curated personas designed to manipulate his favor.","He found the desperation annoying... He wasn’t interested in being surrounded by flatterers.","Jude’s gaze swept over the mob and landed on two girls standing on the periphery of the lobby.","Lyla and Mia hadn’t joined the surge. They were simply watching him with genuine respect.","\"Lyla. Mia,\" Jude’s voice carried across the floor.","The two girls blinked, pointing to themselves in shock.","\"You two will take the first two global headliner spots,\" Jude announced firmly.","The rest of the talent roster gasped, their eyes darting toward the two pop stars.","\"As for the remaining eight spots,\" Jude continued, his gaze sweeping over the crowd of celebrities. \"Apex Media and The Sirens will divide them. I am not interested in your desperate pitches. You will earn those remaining spots through performance metrics and loyalty to this conglomerate. Whoever proves themselves to be the most valuable asset will get the placement. Are we clear?\"","\"Yes, Mr. Lawson!\" the crowd responded.","Lyla and Mia’s faces lit up with excitement.","Without waiting for the mob of celebrities to recover, Jude walked out of the doors, leaving the entertainment industry behind him."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: Conflict of Interest","paragraphs":["Federal Bureau of Investigation, Financial Crimes Division.","A young federal agent stormed into the bullpen, clutching a stack of financial dossiers.","He threw the files down onto his desk, the crack causing everyone in the office to look up from their monitors.","\"We have been investigating Jude Lawson for a month since the Zenith Motors takeover, and this is everything we have?\" the young agent cursed.","\"The man is a ghost,\" one of the forensic accountants sighed, rubbing his temples. \"He rarely leaves a digital trail. The data in those files is the result of us working day and night, tracing routing numbers through Switzerland, the Cayman Islands, and Luxembourg. And every single wire transfer clears international banking regulations perfectly.\"","\"Perfectly?\" the young agent scoffed. \"If a twenty-something kid suddenly drops billions of dollars in liquid cash to execute hostile takeovers of major conglomerates, there has to be a trace of illicit origin somewhere! You don’t just generate billions out of thin air!\"","\"But look at what we’ve actually found!\" the accountant shot back. \"The most serious infractions are aggressive corporate coercion, minor SEC reporting delays, and a few assault charges leveled against some underground fixers who won’t even testify against him!\"","The young agent grew agitated, slamming his hand flat against the desk. \"I refuse to believe Jude Lawson hasn’t gotten his hands dirty with international wire fraud or racketeering in all this time!\"","A hand landed on his shoulder, making him jump.","The young agent turned. \"Supervisory Agent Thorne.\"","The other analysts in the bullpen also rose to their feet. \"Agent Thorne.\"","Saul Thorne, a veteran investigator, gave a nod before looking at the young agent. \"Shouting about it in the bullpen won’t do a damn bit of good. We build federal RICO cases based on hard evidence, and a federal judge signs warrants based on that evidence. We don’t prosecute based on rumors from rival CEOs.\"","\"But Agent Thorne,\" the young investigator pleaded, gesturing at the files. \"With the evidence we have against Lawson right now, he’ll get a minor corporate fine at most. Everyone in the financial sector knows who he is and the leverage he possesses. I can’t believe he doesn’t have a single count of money laundering to his name.\"","Saul Thorne’s reply was calm. \"Evidence. Let the financial ledgers do the talking.\"","\"Agent Thorne, we’ve investigated almost every corporate entity connected to Lawson,\" the forensic accountant interjected, opening a file. \"His inner circle is tight. All the subsidiaries in his name are clean... if there was dirty money, he’s laundered it so thoroughly that the IRS can’t even find a misplaced decimal point.\"","\"Based on the infractions we can prove against Lawson, a federal judge won’t even authorize a subpoena, let alone the confiscation of his corporate empire,\" the young agent muttered bitterly.","These words plunged the Financial Crimes bullpen into silence.","Just then, there was a knock on the door of the bullpen.","\"Agent Thorne,\" a junior agent called out. \"Agent Shepherd’s team just returned from serving a routine inquiry at Apex Studios, that new joint venture Lawson acquired. They brought back someone with close ties to him. Do you want to handle the questioning personally?\"","Saul Thorne nodded firmly. \"I’ll go. Set up Interview Room Four.\"","Inside the interview room, Harper sat in a chair.","She was wearing her vintage denim jacket, looking out of place in the sterile federal building.","A female agent poured her a glass of water from a pitcher.","\"No need to be nervous, Ms. Harper,\" the female agent said. \"This is just a standard interview room, not a hostile interrogation. Just answer truthfully to whatever we ask you in a bit.\"","Harper didn’t look nervous in the slightest. She smiled and nodded, her hands resting on the table.","Soon, footsteps approached from the hallway outside. Agent Shepherd, who had been leaning against the doorframe, straightened up.","The opened, and Saul Thorne walked in, holding a legal notepad.","Their eyes met.","For a moment, Saul Thorne froze in the doorway.","He stared at Harper, his brain convinced he must be hallucinating.","The President of Apex Studios, the billionaire’s newest corporate lieutenant... was his girlfriend?","Harper looked up at him as well. Her expression was simple, almost blank, as if she had expected this exact scene to unfold eventually given his line of work.","\"Agent Thorne?\" Agent Shepherd called out.","Saul Thorne composed himself, his jaw clenching tightly.","He turned to Agent Shepherd. \"I’m recusing myself from this interview.\"","Agent Shepherd nodded.","Saul Thorne gave Harper one long look. He turned on his heel and left the interview room without saying another word.","Agent Shepherd looked at Harper, surprised to find her calm, showing no emotional reaction to her boyfriend’s sudden departure.","Agent Shepherd opened his notepad and began the interview. \"No need to be nervous. Just answer our questions regarding your employer, and you can leave when we’re done.\"","Harper nodded.","Agent Shepherd clicked his pen. \"When did you first meet Jude Lawson?\"","\"Recently,\" Harper answered smoothly.","Agent Shepherd frowned slightly. \"So you’ve only known him for a very short period of time?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You’ve known a billionaire for just a few days, and you are already the President of his multi-billion-dollar film studio? It seems you two have a very unique relationship.\"","\"Yes, we do.\"","Agent Shepherd leaned forward, resting his elbows on the table. \"Are you just business partners who work well together, or is there another kind of relationship privately? Are you romantically involved with the target?\"","\"No,\" Harper smiled faintly. \"He’s my mentor. You could say he’s like a sworn brother to me. He protects my creative vision.\"","Agent Shepherd narrowed his eyes. \"Brother? To your recollection, has Mr. Lawson ever mentioned his past to you? The source of his capital?\"","\"No.\"","\"Not even once? For instance, his struggles coming up in the financial world, the identity of his offshore backers, or any corporate enemies he’s made in the shadows? Nothing?\"","\"No,\" Harper replied, unbothered. \"When we’re together, we discuss our film projects and the studio’s creative direction. I know nothing about his financial past.\"","Harper’s gaze never wavered once.","Her eyes were clear and bright, and her answers came without a single moment’s hesitation, showing no sign of careful deliberation or panic.","The reason Harper was calm was because Jude Lawson had sat her down in the executive lobby just yesterday and given her one guarantee.","\"I will never ask you to lie for me, Harper,\" Jude had told her. \"Anything I tell you is something you can freely repeat to the authorities. Anything you’re not supposed to say, I will simply never tell you in the first place.\"","Because of this promise, Harper knew she didn’t need to lie, and that nothing she said in this room could ever threaten or harm the empire of the man who had changed her life..."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Backing Lexi","paragraphs":["While the federal authorities spun their wheels in utter frustration, Jude was sitting in the back of his Maybach, gliding through the city’s financial district.","He had spent the early morning finalizing the integration of Apex Records and Zenith Motors, but his mind had now shifted back to the digital inventory screen hovering in his vision.","During the Global Soundwave auction, the Platinum Box had awarded him three one-hundred-million-dollar slush funds.","The *Luxury Real Estate* and *Bespoke Assets* funds were straightforward.","The *Digital Media* slush fund stated it could only be routed through live broadcasting platforms, digital content donations, and social media ecosystems.","He needed an avenue to burn through the capital.","Jude pulled out his smartphone and opened his encrypted messaging app, navigating to a contact he hadn’t spoken to since his first week with the system.","Lexi.","She was a high-tier live-streamer who had tried to use Jude for clout.","Jude had humbled her, demonstrating a level of wealth that had left her fiercely loyal.","Jude typed a quick message: *Are there any major broadcast events happening on your network today?*","Ten seconds later, the typing bubble appeared.","Lexi: *Yes! There’s a massive outdoor brand activation and a digital leaderboard tournament today. Do you want me to secure a VIP pass for you?*","Jude: *Is the event highly populated? I need an excuse to clear some digital capital.*","Lexi sent a playful emoji. *Tons of gorgeous streamers will be there. Tell me your type, and I’ll introduce you to the best on the platform.*","Jude chuckled at her pandering. She was an opportunist, but he appreciated the transactional honesty.","Jude: *I’ll pick you up at your agency in twenty minutes. Ensure you are streaming. I am going to back you today.*","Lexi’s reply was a string of excited exclamation points.","Thirty minutes later, the Maybach pulled up to the curb outside of the city’s largest influencer agency.","Lexi was standing on the sidewalk, holding her stabilizing gimbal and streaming to her live chat.","Standing next to her was a younger girl wearing designer streetwear, looking nervously at the massive vehicle.","As Jude stepped out of the Maybach, Lexi beamed.","She hurried over, angling her camera away from Jude’s face to respect his privacy.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" Lexi greeted him. \"Thank you so much for coming. I want you to meet Sienna. She’s a new streamer at my agency, and she’s partnering with me for the outdoor event today.\"","Sienna stepped forward, her eyes wide.","\"Wow,\" Sienna said, looking at Jude with awe. \"Lexi told me her primary backer was a titan, but this is insane. It is an honor to meet you, Boss. Thank you for sponsoring our broadcast today!\"","Sienna’s flattery was so saccharine it bordered on theatrical, but Jude found it refreshing compared to the corporate speak of the Wall Street executives he usually dealt with.","\"Nice to meet you, Sienna,\" Jude said smoothly. \"Get in.\"","Sienna slid into the interior of the Maybach.","As the driver pulled away from the curb, Lexi leaned forward.","\"The event is being hosted at the newly constructed underground luxury promenade,\" Lexi explained, checking her chat feed. \"A dozen high-end designer brands are sponsoring a digital leaderboard. Every major streamer in the city is going to be broadcasting simultaneously from the promenade. The streamer who generates the highest volume of digital donations during the two-hour window wins the grand prize... a massive corporate sponsorship payout.\"","\"And you want the payout?\" Jude asked.","\"We don’t care about the brand payout,\" Sienna chimed in, shaking her head. \"We just want the agency bonus! Our streaming network gives a fifty-thousand-dollar cash bonus to whichever of their streamers takes first place on the overall leaderboard.\"","Lexi nodded eagerly. \"Exactly! The clout of placing first on the regional leaderboard is worth ten times the brand payout for our channel metrics.\"","Jude smiled. If they wanted first place, they were going to get it...","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Digital Supremacy.]","[Objective: The digital landscape is simply another arena for capital dominance. Secure the absolute first-place ranking on the live broadcast leaderboard and humiliate the opposition.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","The mission didn’t even require effort. Jude had a hundred-million-dollar slush fund literally burning a hole in his system inventory.","It wasn’t a matter of if he would win, but by how many millions he would shatter the existing platform records...","Ten minutes later, the Maybach descended into the VIP parking garage of the luxury promenade.","The moment Jude, Lexi, and Sienna stepped out of the private elevator banks and onto the main promenade, it was obvious the event was already in full swing.","The walkway was swarming with dozens of streamers holding selfie sticks and ring lights.","However, two crowds had formed near the center of the promenade, dominating the foot traffic.","At the epicenter stood two of the most famous influencers on the continent.","One was \"Titan,\" a loud hype-streamer whose channel boasted over five million active subscribers.","The other was \"Vixen,\" a beauty guru whose audience was equally massive.","Titan was currently holding his camera high above his head, shouting into the microphone while his fans screamed in the background.","\"Listen up, chat!\" Titan roared, flexing his arms. \"You already know how this leaderboard is going to end! I’ve teamed up with the Queen herself, Vixen! Our channels are linked for the donation drive!\"","Titan turned and pointed mockingly at the dozens of smaller streamers hovering on the periphery of the crowd.","\"To all the other streamers in the building, I suggest you just pack up your ring lights and go home!\" Titan boasted. \"Vixen and I are taking first and second place on the leaderboard today. It’s a mathematical certainty! You can all fight over the scraps for third place!\"","The smaller streamers exchanged looks. It was demoralizing...","Titan and Vixen had millions of fans.","Competing against their combined digital ecosystem was impossible for a mid-tier streamer.","Vixen flipped her hair, barely glancing at the crowd. \"Don’t even try to snipe the top spot, guys. Our whales are locked and loaded. The leaderboard is closed.\"","Lexi gritted her teeth, her grip tightening on her gimbal. \"They are so arrogant. Titan always pulls this stunt.\"","Sienna, however, was not intimidated...","She had just ridden in a Maybach with a billionaire.","Sienna stepped forward, cupping her hands around her mouth.","\"You guys can have third place!\" Sienna yelled back across the floor. \"Because our Patron is taking first place for us today!\"","Titan paused his broadcast, lowering his camera.","He turned his head, his eyes narrowing as he locked onto Sienna.","Vixen stopped touching up her makeup, glaring at the new girl."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: Walking Away Clean","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, across the city at the Federal Bureau of Investigation, Harper answered every question honestly and conscientiously...","She didn’t hide what she knew regarding the creative operations at Apex Studios, nor did she say a word more than necessary about what she didn’t.","Her demeanor made it abundantly clear to Agent Shepherd that she wasn’t lying.","Supervisory Agent Saul Thorne leaned against the cinderblock wall of the federal corridor, his gaze fixed on the door of Interview Room Four.","His career in the Financial Crimes division required clinical detachment. But today, an uncontrollable tightness constricted his chest, and his mind was a mess.","Harper had never mentioned Jude Lawson in front of him. Not a single word.","He had never imagined that Harper, an indie filmmaker who preferred vintage thrift stores to corporate boardrooms, would have any connection to a corporate raider like Lawson.","Time ticked by... The initial shock slowly gave way to fear.","He was afraid that Jude Lawson’s shadow-laced financial empire would truly implicate Harper.","He was even more afraid that she would cover for Lawson and become a federal accomplice!","About forty minutes later, the door of Interview Room Four finally opened.","Agent Shepherd was the first to emerge. He looked up, adjusting his tie, and saw Saul Thorne waiting by the door. He walked over and spoke in a low voice.","\"Agent Thorne, we’ve asked everything we needed to regarding her appointment,\" Agent Shepherd said. \"We didn’t find anything suspicious. Your girlfriend and Jude Lawson appear to have a protective brother-sister dynamic, but she genuinely doesn’t know much about his offshore financial affairs.\"","Saul Thorne’s pupils constricted. Brother and sister... this was obviously not just ordinary corporate employment!","\"You had no idea she was the President of his studio?\" Agent Shepherd asked, reading Saul’s expression.","Saul Thorne shook his head, a hollow feeling settling in his stomach.","Agent Shepherd sighed.","He reached out, patted Saul’s shoulder, and tried to comfort him. \"You need to try and relax about this, Saul. The division will be investigating your girlfriend’s corporate footprint closely. If she isn’t found to be harboring his illicit funds, you don’t need to take this so seriously.\"","Soon, Harper also came out of the room, escorted by the female agent. Her expression was serene.","Agent Shepherd knew Saul Thorne would have things to say to his girlfriend, so he gave them space, beckoning the female agent to leave the corridor with him.","Saul Thorne looked at Harper, struggling to find his voice, but ultimately, he didn’t know what to say.","Harper smiled faintly. \"Walk me out first.\"","They walked out of the federal building side by side. Saul Thorne didn’t reach out to take her hand, but Harper felt no sense of loss at the distance between them.","She knew Saul Thorne, and she understood the nature of his badge.","Saul Thorne didn’t stop walking until they were out the main entrance, standing on the steps under the overcast city sky. He looked at Harper, his expression complex, and finally spoke.","\"Why didn’t you tell me?\" Saul demanded.","Harper tilted her head up slightly to look at him.","To this day, she had never tired of looking at Saul Thorne’s face...","It was still just as handsome and sharply defined as when they had first met.","But at this precise moment, she was more clear-headed than she had ever been in her entire life.","\"I’m not a suspect, Saul, much less a criminal. I have no obligation to come clean to you about my employment or my corporate benefactors,\" Harper said, her tone remarkably calm. \"Besides, my relationship with him is my own personal affair. It has nothing to do with anyone else in this building, and I’m not obligated to tell anyone about it.\"","A flash of pain crossed Saul Thorne’s eyes, his voice rising in desperation. \"But he’s not a good person, Harper! He is a ruthless corporate raider! You’re so close to him, you had to have known he destroys companies and ruins lives!\"","\"I understand what you mean.\" Harper nodded, her tone shifted, hardening slightly. \"But everyone in this world has their own unique perspective from which they view people and things.\"","Saul stared at her, bewildered.","\"From your point of view at the Bureau, of course he’s a bad man,\" Harper continued. \"From the point of view of Wall Street, and maybe even most of the corporate world, he’s a monster. But to the artists he protects... to the people he elevates from nothing... and from my point of view... he’s a good brother and an incredible mentor.\"","Saul Thorne’s expression twisted into agony.","And Harper knew of Saul Thorne’s dedication to his identity as a federal agent.","So she gave a smile and said, \"Saul, I’ve been very happy during my time with you. But now, we both know it’s over.\"","From the very beginning, all she had wanted was a simple romance...","But now, Jude Lawson was like a thorn that would forever be stuck in Saul Thorne’s heart.","Once a rift of this magnitude formed between them, the relationship would no longer be pure but would instead become complicated by federal subpoenas and mutual suspicion.","Harper would never let herself get trapped in such a compromised relationship. She had to get out now.","Because she would not sever ties with Jude Lawson for Saul Thorne. Even if the federal government managed to freeze Jude’s assets or put him on trial, she still had to manage Apex Studios for him.","Furthermore, the classified documents regarding the studio’s creative equity division and several of Jude’s private assets were resting in her safe.","This was Jude Lawson’s trust in her, and she would not betray it.","Saul Thorne looked at Harper, the words to ask her to stay caught in his throat.","If she said it was over, then it was over.","After a long silence, Harper knew Saul Thorne had accepted the end of their relationship. She looked at him, her smile still warm.","\"I know you and your division will continue to investigate me and the studio. You’re a good federal agent; it’s your duty,\" Harper said softly. \"Be it me, or Jude... if that day ever comes where you have to cross that line... I won’t blame you.\"","\"Harper...\" Saul Thorne murmured.","Harper just shook her head.","\"Goodbye, Saul Thorne.\"","Harper turned and walked away down the steps without looking back.","Saul Thorne stood rooted to the spot, watching her figure recede into the distance until she disappeared around the corner.","Bound by his badge and his pride, he still didn’t say the words to make her stay...","Meanwhile, Harper got into her vintage car parked at the curb.","Sitting in the driver’s seat, she let out a sigh.","The sudden end of the relationship didn’t seem to have a devastating impact on her; she just felt deep down that it was a genuine shame.","But as she pulled away from the curb, heading back toward the monolith of Apex Media, her mind was at peace. Her loyalty belonged to Jude Lawson."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: A Visit to the Backlot","paragraphs":["Her phone suddenly vibrated against the passenger seat.","The encrypted caller ID simply read: *Boss.*","Harper collected her thoughts, took a deep breath, and answered the call through the car’s Bluetooth system.","\"Jude?\"","Jude Lawson paused for a fraction of a second before speaking, his voice calm. \"Are you out of the federal building?\"","\"I just got out.\" Harper forced a laugh and asked, \"Did Director Vance panic and tell you?\"","\"Did the agents give you a hard time?\" Jude ignored her question.","\"No, I just answered whatever they asked.\" As Harper spoke. \"Jude, I finally understand why you gave me that speech in the lobby yesterday. When I was sitting in that interrogation room, I was calm. My conscience was clear. I didn’t have to worry that my words might trigger a perjury charge, and I didn’t have to consider whether I should lie to cover for your offshore accounts.\"","\"Lying to a federal agent and committing perjury carry severe prison sentences,\" Jude replied. \"You run my studio, Harper, so I have an obligation to protect you. I will not let you get legally implicated in my broader acquisitions.\"","\"Besides,\" Jude added. \"I’ve already entrusted you with the majority of Apex Media’s creative equity. There’s a selfish reason for me to protect your public record, so don’t overthink the sentimentality. If the FBI ever does manage to find traction on me, you’ll be the one keeping the studio alive.\"","\"That’s all for now,\" Jude said. \"Maya will contact you this afternoon regarding the transfer of our new global broadcasting assets. Harper... take care of yourself.\"","After hanging up the call, Harper sat in the idling car.","Without a hesitation, she took out her phone, opened her contacts, and deleted all information related to Saul Thorne.","...","Apex Studios Headquarters.","Several weeks later, Isabella Frost... one of the studio’s fastest-rising young actresses knocked lightly on the door of Connie’s office.","\"Well, look who it is! Isabella?\"","Connie, a veteran talent manager, was surprised to see her star client.","She put down her tablet and stood up to greet her warmly. \"You’ve been quiet for the last month in your acting workshops. What brings you to the executive floor all of a sudden?\"","Isabella smiled, returning the greeting before explaining her reason for coming. \"Connie, I’ve finished reading that script you sent me last week, and I’ve made my final decision.\"","Connie’s eyes lit up at her words. \"You’re willing to take it?\"","Isabella nodded.","\"That’s more like it! I told you you’d be deeply interested in the character once you actually read the script. It’ll be a whole new creative challenge for you.\"","\"The character is what drew me in,\" Isabella admitted, sitting down in the chair. \"I want to give it a try, but I just don’t know if I can do her justice on screen.\"","Connie happily took Isabella’s hands to encourage her. \"No problem at all! Plus, this is a serious prestige drama. Mr. Lawson has authorized a massive budget for it, so most of the main and supporting cast are veteran A-listers with superb skills. If you can get on this production, you’re guaranteed to learn a lot.\"","\"Did Heather Keaton take the part?\" Isabella asked hopefully.","\"Of course she did. How could a veteran turn down such a phenomenal script?\" Connie said with a wide smile. \"This way, she’ll be the female lead, and you’ll be the second female lead. Since you’re both my clients under the Apex umbrella, she can look out for you on set.\"","Hearing this, Isabella’s lips curved into a delighted smile.","\"So if you’re sure you’re taking it, I’ll confirm the casting with the production team right now!\" Connie said, reaching for her phone.","\"Okay. By the way, Connie, I heard the *Crimson Dynasty* crew is filming on the Apex backlot recently. I want to go visit Yuna and Finn.\"","While Isabella had been on a month-long break for her immersive acting workshops, the company had assigned her two personal assistants, Yuna and Finn, to other artists to keep them on the payroll.","Connie nodded. \"No problem. I think they’re currently assigned to Rachel Farris’s team right now. Do you need me to give her manager a heads-up?\"","\"That would be great. It would be a little rude to just show up to her set unannounced.\"","Connie smiled. \"I’ll let them know now. I’ll print you a VIP pass for the backlot in a bit, and you can take a golf cart straight there.\"","After leaving the executive tower, Isabella grabbed an iced coffee and headed directly out to the studio backlot.","On the way, she sent a quick text message to Yuna ahead of time, but she never got a reply.","Getting through the security checkpoints was easy with the VIP pass.","Isabella quickly navigated the maze of soundstages and found the outdoor set for *Crimson Dynasty*.","\"Ms. Frost?\"","She ran into a production assistant at the entrance to the set. \"What are you doing all the way out here? Are you slated for a cameo?\"","Isabella denied it, smiling politely. \"No, no, I’m just here to visit the set.\"","She tapped her VIP pass against the lanyard on her chest as she spoke.","\"Oh, who are you here to see? They’re filming an exterior shot inside. Let me take you in!\"","\"I’m here to see Yuna and Finn. They’re my personal assistants,\" Isabella explained. \"I’ve been on a workshop break, so the company assigned them to Ms. Farris’s team to keep their hours up.\"","\"Oh...\" The man nodded in understanding. \"I think I just saw Ms. Farris over at Exterior Stage 1. Let me take you inside first.\"","\"Thank you!\"","It was a Victorian-era drama, and the background actors on set were all wearing period costumes.","When they reached a spot behind the camera tracks, the man pointed to a canopy not far away and whispered, \"Ms. Frost, Ms. Farris is over there. See? Is that your assistant, Yuna, next to her?\"","Isabella followed his finger and looked over.","She saw Rachel Farris, dressed in modern casual clothes, reclining lazily on a rocking chair underneath the shade of a production tent.","Yuna, however, was not under the tent.","Yuna was standing out in the direct sunlight, holding a UV umbrella over Rachel with one hand and a fan with the other, half-squatting just to shield the older actress from the glare.","The outdoor temperature had reached ninety-five degrees, yet Yuna herself was exposed to the sun.","Sweat poured down her face, and her skin was much darker than the last time Isabella had seen her.","Not only that, but a backpack was slung over Yuna’s shoulder...","Yuna’s body was shaking, looking ready to collapse at any moment.","Meanwhile, other actors were also resting on the sidelines between takes, but they had all found shady spots to sit.","Even those accompanied by assistants were, at most, just being handed water bottles or scripts when they needed them.","Isabella’s heart sank, and a surge of anger washed over her."]}]);
